st to September came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those 75 years. In 2025, April to May ran 172% of normal on the middle of the grids, while November to December ran 51%. The 2026 numbers published so far start low, with January to February at 46% and February to March at 49%. Every grid had its driest year in 2010, and grid 16649 bottomed out at 62% that year.</p>"}
